-- title:
--   Transition isomorphisms of smooth local lifts on overlaps
-- statement:
--   Let $\pi\colon T'\to T$ be a surjective homomorphism of commutative rings whose kernel is a nilpotent ideal, let $f_0\colon A_0\to\operatorname{Spec} T$ be a separated morphism of schemes, and let $\mathcal U$ be an ordered affine cover of $A_0$, i.e. a finite linearly ordered index type $\iota$ together with opens $U_a\subseteq A_0$, each affine, with $\bigvee_a U_a=\top$. Assume given, for each $a$, a smooth morphism $q_a\colon Y_a\to\operatorname{Spec} T'$ and a morphism $g_a\colon U_a\to Y_a$ making the square formed by $g_a$, the composite $U_a\hookrightarrow A_0\to\operatorname{Spec} T$, $q_a$ and $\operatorname{Spec}\pi$ cartesian, and an assignment $O_a$ from opens of $A_0$ to opens of $Y_a$ with: $g_a^{-1}O_a(W)$ equal to the preimage of $W$ in $U_a$; $O_a$ monotone; $O_a(U_a)=\top$; $O_a(W)\wedge O_a(W')\le O_a(W\wedge W')$; and $O_a(W)$ affine whenever $W\le U_a$ is affine. The conclusion asserts the existence of isomorphisms $\varphi_{ab}\colon O_a(U_a\wedge U_b)\cong O_b(U_a\wedge U_b)$ for all $a<b$ such that: $\varphi_{ab}$ followed by the inclusion of $O_b(U_a\wedge U_b)$ into $Y_b$ and $q_b$ equals the corresponding structure morphism of $O_a(U_a\wedge U_b)$; the restrictions of $g_a$ and $g_b$ to $U_a\wedge U_b$ factor through the two opens by morphisms $\gamma,\gamma'$ with $\gamma$ followed by $\varphi_{ab}$ equal to $\gamma'$; and for every open $W\subseteq A_0$ the $\varphi_{ab}$-preimage of $O_b(W)\cap O_b(U_a\wedge U_b)$ is $O_a(W)\cap O_a(U_a\wedge U_b)$. Furthermore, for each triple overlap, indexed by a strictly monotone $r\colon\{0,1,2\}\to\iota$ with $U_r=\bigwedge_j U_{r(j)}$, there are isomorphisms $\rho^{r}_{ab},\rho^{r}_{bc},\rho^{r}_{ac}$ between the corresponding $O_{r(j)}(U_r)$, compatible with $\varphi_{r(0)r(1)}$, $\varphi_{r(1)r(2)}$, $\varphi_{r(0)r(2)}$ through the inclusions coming from monotonicity of the $O$'s, and such that, reading $O_{r(0)}(U_r)$ through its isomorphism with $\operatorname{Spec}\Gamma(Y_{r(0)},O_{r(0)}(U_r))$ and equipping that ring with the $T'$-algebra structure induced by $q_{r(0)}$: both $\rho^{r}_{ac}$ and the composite $\rho^{r}_{ab}$ followed by $\rho^{r}_{bc}$, followed by the inclusion into $Y_{r(2)}$ and $q_{r(2)}$, equal $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $T'\to\Gamma(Y_{r(0)},O_{r(0)}(U_r))$; and the two composites become equal after precomposition with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the quotient by the ideal generated by the image of $\ker\pi$ in $\Gamma(Y_{r(0)},O_{r(0)}(U_r))$.
--
--   This is the transition-datum step in the deformation-theoretic construction of lifts of a separated $T$-scheme along a surjection $T'\to T$ with nilpotent kernel: local smooth lifts over the members of an ordered affine cover are unique up to isomorphism, and the resulting isomorphisms on pairwise overlaps, restricted to triple overlaps, agree modulo the kernel ideal. It is used by the construction of the two-cocycle obstruction valued in point derivations, [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.exists_pointDerivations_obstruction_two_cocycle_of_local_lifts`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmallExtension.exists_pointDerivations_obstruction_two_cocycle_of_local_lifts).
